course: dictionary
lesson: 12748
title: Dud
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A dud is something that does not work properly. «The firework was a dud: it fizzed, but it did not go off.» The clue is did not go off, so dud means useless or failed.
explain: Dud is an informal word, so you hear it in everyday talk. «The new torch was a dud because the batteries were flat.» Something that is a dud has let you down.
explain: A dud can also be a person or thing that disappoints. «The sequel turned out to be a dud.» Here dud means it was a big disappointment.
explain: Safety comes first. Never pick up a dud firework, because it may still go off. Leave it alone and tell an adult.
fact: «Dud» is an informal word, so it is used in chatty speech more than in formal writing.
fact: A dud can be a noun, as in «a dud», or an adjective, as in «a dud battery».
fact: «Turned out to be a dud» means it failed or disappointed people.
fact: A military dud is a bomb or shell that did not explode.
fact: Never pick up a dud firework, because it may still go off.
exercise: «The firework was a dud and did not go off.» What is a dud? | A tool for cutting paper | A loud bang in the sky | *Something that does not work properly | A bright star that stays lit all night
exercise: Sam says, «The film was a dud, so boring.» What does dud mean here? | A film in a foreign language | A new and exciting film | A very long film with lots of songs | *A disappointment
exercise: You find a firework on the ground that did not go off. What is the safe thing to do? | *Leave it alone and tell an adult | Shake it to see if it rattles | Light it again to check | Pick it up to see why it failed
test:
In «a dud battery», what part of speech is dud? | Noun | *Adjective | Verb | Adverb
What does «turned out to be a dud» mean? | It was very loud | *It failed or disappointed | It was very old | It was made of cloth
exam:
Which of these is a dud? | A bag full of new clothes | A bright sunny day at the beach | *A shell that was fired but did not explode | A cup of hot cocoa
